racts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1818383/000181838326000200/0001818383-26-000200-index.htm","accession":"0001818383-26-000200"},{"text":"Gross margin is only 14.3%, so scale has to be enormous before anything reaches the bottom line.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001818383"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 10.6% over the year (Q2 2026 vs Q2 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1818383/000181838326000200/0001818383-26-000200-index.htm","accession":"0001818383-26-000200"},{"text":"Debt of $176.7m against equity of $28.4m. Leverage decides who controls the outcome if trading deteriorates, and it is not the shareholder.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1818383/000181838326000200/0001818383-26-000200-index.htm","accession":"0001818383-26-000200"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 14.2% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (716,243 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1818383/000181838326000202/0001818383-26-000202-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 6.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.06,"consecutive":2,"current":0.143,"current_display":"14.3%","threshold_display":"6.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarte